id=a52sxq_devicecare_sleep_lists
name=Device Care: list every restrictable app in the sleeping app lists
author=CodesRahul96
description=Battery > Background usage limits > Sleeping / Deep sleeping / Never auto sleeping apps > Add. (1) The Add lists use canRestrictWithReason instead of canRestrict and ignore only its widget (0x8) and quick panel tile (0x100000) bits (canRestrict also applied the server deep sleep exception list and adjust-restriction 21). (2) MARs only manages apps that have a row in SDHMS' ForcedAppStandby table and SDHMS never gives one to an app on the doze allowlist (Battery "Unrestricted"), so such apps were in none of the lists and restrict() on them did nothing. User-installed apps on the user doze allowlist are now offered under Sleeping and Deep sleeping apps (not Never auto sleeping: they are already exempt). Adding one takes it off the allowlist (= Battery "Optimized"), inserts its FAS row the way SDHMS does on install, waits up to 4 s until MARs manages it and, for deep sleep, re-checks MARs' own protections (device admin, default apps, keyboard, wallpaper, contact-sync accounts, protected packages) before the stock code restricts it; on a veto or when MARs has not picked it up within 4 s the allowlist entry is restored (back to Unrestricted, not added). When the add comes from Device Care's UI thread and the list holds an allowlisted app, that preparation runs on a background thread and the stock restrict code then runs on the UI thread with the prepared list, so the screen never waits for it (the list updates when it is done); adds without allowlisted apps stay synchronous as in stock. Apps that re-allowlist themselves (Samsung platform-signed Good Lock modules with DEVICE_POWER) leave the list again when they next start.
